{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"chilled-bereaved-equine","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# The step-budget repetition diagnostic is computed, then dropped\n\nDiscovered while root-causing [rebar:bf31-fd55-d28d-4b7a]. The reported symptom was \"the gate cannot\nbe tuned because it cannot be observed\" — no partial verdict, no count of anything, just a bare\nbudget number. The diagnostic that answers it **already exists** and is thrown away one frame from\nthe surface.\n\n`interpret_failure` (`src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:79-101`) builds `budget_diag` via\n`usage_log.failure_usage`, which reduces every tool call to a `(tool_name, sha256(args)[:8])`\nsignature and summarizes it — `tool_calls_distinct`, `max_consecutive_repeat`,\n`top_repeated_tool_calls`. That is precisely the loop-vs-explore discriminator\n(`src/rebar/llm/usage_log.py:147-157` documents exactly this intent), and it is attached as\n`budget_err.diagnostic`.\n\nIt then goes nowhere. `emit_gate_error` is only called by `raise_completion_workflow_failure` when\n`failure_diagnostic` is truthy (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:382-403`), and\n`failure_diagnostic` is set ONLY inside `CompletionAgentStep._recover` — which a budget exhaustion\nnever reaches (see the sibling recovery-reachability ticket). So **no `gate_error_v1` sidecar is\nwritten** and the CLI message carries none of it. In the instrumented reproduction the propagated\nexception reached the caller with `diagnostic: null`.\n\nTwo operators burned ~50 minutes each escalating the budget 480 -> 1600 against a constraint that\nwas never a budget. The measurement that would have said so in one line was computed on the first\nrun and discarded.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a step-budget exhaustion writes a `gate_error_v1` sidecar carrying the repetition summary\n      (`requests`, `tool_calls`, `tool_calls_distinct`, `max_consecutive_repeat`,\n      `top_repeated_tool_calls`)\n- [ ] the operator-facing close-gate message includes the distinct-vs-total tool-call counts, so\n      \"it looped\" is distinguishable from \"it ran out of room\" without reading a log\n- [ ] the sidecar payload stays free of prompts, tool arguments and response text (the existing\n      privacy contract in `usage_log.failure_usage` is preserved)\n- [ ] a test asserts the sidecar is emitted and its counters are populated for a budget exhaustion","id":"8b97-a0ca-82a4-4d4e","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Step-budget repetition diagnostic is computed then dropped: no gate_error_v1 sidecar, no counters in the operator message"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785932640392378001,"uuid":"5e94da9a-56f4-4cc9-ae3c-4b2df0a94d2d"}